+### 6.2 R5 — Road encounter (existing): band map & beat routing
+
+**File:** `Elderwyld/Roads/mireward_reach_road_d100_encounter_table.md`  
+**Roll:** Player rolls **d100** (or d10 within band — see below).  
+**Escalation rule (from file):** Same band twice → raise stakes; don't repeat verbatim.
+
+**Thematic order (how the d100 is structured):**
+
+| Rows | Band title | Theme (what this slice of the list is *for*) | Count |
+|------|------------|-----------------------------------------------|-------|
+| **01–10** | Crown, Mud, and Maintenance | Maintained road reality — ditches, mile-markers, crown crews, mud economics | 10 |
+| **11–20** | Traffic, Convoys, and Strangers | People on the move — refugees, merchants, riders, fame spillover from Mirathorn | 10 |
+| **21–30** | Weather, Sky, and Shimmer | Storm inheritance — savory rain, static, mirage, hail, wrong lightning | 10 |
+| **31–40** | Hamlets, Inns, and Half-Truths | Settled texture — waystations, clerks, local lies, capacity strain | 10 |
+| **41–50** | Predators, Press, and Petty Cruelty | Teeth and tolls — beasts, bandits-lite, road cruelty (keep quick) | 10 |
+| **51–60** | Shepherd's Shadow (Subtle) | North undertone — wrong meat, choir wells, chalk signs; **not** sermons | 10 |
+| **61–70** | Forks, Fences, and Bad Maps | Navigation friction — bad advice, washed bridges, fence politics | 10 |
+| **71–80** | Liminal Weird | Strange without mandatory fight — lights, lines, hearsay | 10 |
+| **81–100** | Hard Turns (Major Beats) | **Larger** beats — abandoned places, major forks, campaign-weight discoveries | **20** |
+
+**Beat band windows (player rolls d100; reroll once if outside window, then take closest in-window row):**
+
+| March beat | In-world | **Allowed R5 rows** | Narrative intent |
+|------------|----------|----------------------|------------------|
+| **1** | Days 1–2, storm chapter | **01–30** | Maintenance + traffic + **weather** — Reach is real; storm continues S21 |
+| **2** | Day 3, north pressure | **11–60** | Strangers + hamlets + **Shepherd undertone** — unease without arrival |
+| **3** | Day 4, approach | **11–40** or **31–70** *(pick one window for session; document in journey tracker)* | Refugee traffic + failing waystations + navigation — **smell before walls** |
+| **4** | Day 5, arrival | **No R5 by default** — use **§10** + **T-DIL-G** | Save road table for epilogue travel if session runs long |
+
+**Alternate procedure (clearer at table):** GM announces beat band → player rolls **d10** → GM reads row `(band_start + d10 - 1)` except band **81–100** uses **d20** on rows 81–100.
+
+**Do not:** Chain multiple R5 rolls per day unless players choose to linger. **Do not:** GM curate “best” row — reroll only on band miss or duplicate verbatim (per R5 escalation rule).
