+      "rendered_text": "# Planning Question\n\nShepherd's Flock cult — Maelthor, tainted meat, music conversion, Dustwalker, and cult pressure north toward fen and swamp (Campaign 2).\n\n# Retrieval and Authority Summary\n\n- Retrieval mode: prior_only\n- Admission policy: lane_budgeted_v1\n- Grading context: admitted_context\n- Support knowledge allowed: no\n- Oracle material allowed: no\n- Candidate depth: 50\n- Admitted context items: 48\n- Estimated rendered tokens: 1555\n\n# Known Gaps and Safety Constraints\n\n- (none)\n\n# Support / Adaptation Context\n\n- (none)\n\n# Prior Campaign Memory\n\n- [meta-session-0021-open-loops] session unresolved open questions loops open loops actionable follow up next session mirathorn_festival_resumed Mirathorn resumed the Festival; Frank hung up; Lysandra cannot get through — is the city compromised or merely distracted? elderwyld cities and towns cities and towns mirathorn swamp_vs_mirathorn_fork Party agreed to press on to the swamp rather than turn back — S22 opening pressure. longmont campaign longmont campaign campaign 2 parties questionable company questionable company\n- [u-L0003-14] They warn the sheriff about tainted meat and Karsemine uses her Thaumaturgy to show them what to look for when people begin to change.\n- [u-L0021-07] Caelynn calls Sara to tell her the good news about Lysandra, and bad news about the tainted meat.\n- [u-L0005-08] After conferring with Lysandra, they determine that they are 3 days from Mirathorn and the next little town north along the road will be Mireward, about 5 days out.\n- [u-L0017-07] Lysandra tells her that she can't remember much after the group left, only that she decided to go around the forest and she could smell meat while trying to sleep.\n- [u-L0019-07] The first thing Caelynn notices about Lysandra is that her eyes are shimmery, just like the members of the cult.\n- [u-L0021-03] Stafl starts sorting through the provisions, convinced that someone snuck in the tainted meat before leaving Mirathorn.\n- [u-L0003-06] Stafl and Lysandra, both in need of a good rest, lay down in the back of the wagon, using this time to recharge while they travel.\n- [u-L0005-06] They leave the wagon and the animals at the bottom and make their way up until they reach a giant bowl of water surrounded by a grove of trees.\n- [u-L0007-07] The top of the hill is again shaped like a giant bowl, just as before, but this time instead of water this bowl is filled with detritus and the horrible smell of decay.\n- [u-L0007-08] Karsemine sneaks back to the group and warns them that something is definitely living here.\n- [u-L0007-09] Bonogo does not want to leave without taking a look himself, so Karsemine casts Pass Without a Trace and they both sneak back up.\n- [u-L0007-10] They slowly make their way back through the remaining brush to the lip of the bowl and suddenly Bonogo is overwhelmed with the scent of reptiles.\n- [u-L0009-03] Based on their size five of these would be a tough battle for the group, so it doesn't look good if they are caught fighting the whole nest.\n- [u-L0009-04] Bonogo decides now is a good time to check again on how many remained in the nest.\n- [u-L0009-05] What he finds is nine young drakes remain, but he also discovers two large elder drakes and seven more sitting on smaller nests.\n- [u-L0009-06] Because of the spell from Karsemine he is able to sneak even closer without being seen.\n- [u-L0011-01] Stafl is on first watch, with little happening, until the sky darkens further and he can just make out a huge swarm of wings.\n- [u-L0011-05] He apologizes to her, telling Caelynn that the city resumed the Festival and it was a long night.\n- [u-L0011-08] And things don't appear to be improving.\n- [u-L0011-09] In need of a friend, she approaches Lysandra to tell her what just happened, but Lysandra doesn't appear to notice that Caelynn is barely holding back tears.\n- [u-L0011-11] Lysandra then notices Ephanna talking with her while she is brewing some tea.\n- [u-L0011-12] She takes the chance to approach Caelynn again and asks for some tea and finally notices the state that Caelynn is in.\n- [u-L0011-13] Now it's Lysandra's turn to burst into tears.\n- [u-L0011-14] After collecting herself, she tells Caelynn that she has done a little investigation into the person they spoke about back in the city and how she finally sees how much the group does for her.\n- [u-L0013-01] Ephanna moves in to speak with Lysandra and tell her about the earlier call to Mirathorn.\n- [u-L0013-02] Lysandra decides to make a call herself, but does not even get an answer.\n- [u-L0013-04] Now the group must decide: continue on their mission to the swamp, or turn back and see what is happening at the city.\n- [u-L0013-05] After a brief discussion, they agree to press on to the swamp.\n- [u-L0013-07] Marla then grapples Bonogo and is about to do much worse when Caelynn comes to the rescue.\n- [u-L0015-03] Immediately they can all see the trees pull back and then start to turn to the east, away from the town.\n- [u-L0015-04] Cheers go up along the ditches and into town.\n- [u-L0015-05] The mayor and sheriff congratulate the heroes and thank them again for all their help.\n- [u-L0015-06] Marla approaches Caelynn and asks her how she should deal with Bonogo, but Ephanna quickly intervenes, letting her, and the town, know that the Questionable Company is leaving town to continue their journey.\n- [u-L0015-07] And now that the danger has passed Caelynn asks the mayor about Lysandra, but finds out that they have never heard of her.\n- [u-L0017-01] Caelynn quickly pulls out the \"rockie-talkie\" and attempts to call Lysandra.\n- [u-L0017-03] Caelynn relays her request and Sara calls Lysandra.\n- [u-L0017-04] She tells Caelynn that all she could hear was mumbling about the forest leaving and that something strange happened to the time.\n- [u-L0017-05] Sara then connects Caelynn directly to Lysandra who is relieved and overjoyed that the group is ok and that they took care of the forest.\n- [u-L0017-06] Caelynn wants to know if she is ok and where she is.\n- [u-L0017-08] She is exhausted and disoriented.\n- [u-L0017-09] Caelynn tells her to stop where she is and make a camp and rest, Karesmine will lead the team to her.\n- [u-L0019-01] Using her extensive tracking skills, Karesmine is able to estimate the distance and direction that Lysandra may have traveled.\n- [u-L0019-04] Caelynn approaches the makeshift shelter and hears mumbling from inside.\n- [u-L0019-05] She finds Lysandra drawing in the dirt.\n- [u-L0019-06] She says it is a tower where the voices are coming from and she knows where it is.\n- [u-L0019-11] Finally, after drinking the tea, Lysandra comes out of the spell.\n- [u-L0019-12] She is very confused, wondering where she is and how she got there.\n\n# Character / Party Behavior Context\n\n- (none)\n\n# Location / Worldbuilding Context\n\n- (none)\n\n# Provenance Map\n\n- meta-session-0021-open-loops: {'ref': 'meta-session-0021-open-loops', 'unit_id': 'meta-session-0021-open-loops', 'source_kind': None, 'source_layer': None, 'source_path': None, 'source_recap_path': 'Longmont Campaign/Campaign 2/Session Recaps/_normalized/Session 21 - Drake Nest Mirathorn Call.md', 'source_reference': None, 'subject_class': None, 'subject_id': None, 'section_heading': None, 'planner_lane_hint': None, 'presentation_lane': 'prior_campaign_memory', 'admission_budget_lane': 'prior_campaign_memory', 'candidate_rank': 1, 'admitted_rank': 1, 'rendered_section_id': 'prior_campaign_memory', 'admission_reason': 'lane_target_prior_campaign_memory', 'merge_reason': None, 'merge_family': None, 'route_reason': 'presentation_lane_prior_campaign_memory', 'evidence_scope': None, 'basis': None, 'gap': None}\n- u-L0003-06: {'ref': 'u-L0003-06', 'unit_id': 'u-L0003-06', 'source_kind': None, 'source_layer': None, 'source_path': None, 'source_recap_path': 'Longmont Campaign/Campaign 2/Session Recaps/_normalized/Session 